# will_path — a will plans its way to its target, attends to the way, and proposes only the next step
#
# Lockpicking is a will: it wants unlock_door and nothing else. Standing in the Test Field with a
# hairpin, the only lock in reach is the Test Door, off the yard — two steps: walk to the yard, then
# unlock it (`inspect will` reads the plan ActionPathPlanner made).
#
# Field: the phase is pinned to the yard (`observe`), the one object here offering the path's first
# step. Observing it WITH lockpicking keeps the focus and gives the path as the reason.
# Thinking with lockpicking on the yard proposes the walk. The walk is a step on the way, not what the
# will wants, so its means is judged like any goal's: pinned here to Woodcraft (`means`). Yard: the
# door opens the phase; thinking with lockpicking proposes the unlock, which a will with the Action
# function carries out itself, whatever the means pin says; the hairpin is combined and the door opens.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm lockpicking,woodcraft --grant-item hairpin --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
observe "Test Yard"
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will lockpicking steps=2 first="
expect-state will "unlock and open the test door"

# Observing with the will: the yard is on its way, so it keeps it, and the reason is the path.
click keyword yard
choose 1
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
expect Through it I could

# Thinking with the will on the yard: the first step, voiced as the way to the goal, by the judged means.
means woodcraft
click keyword yard
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
expect To get there I must first
expect so I will
expect [Woodcraft

strategy succeed
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state where Test Yard
expect-state will "will lockpicking steps=1"

# The next phase is clicked into: settle the word-vector load first (see `wait embeddings`).
wait embeddings 60
observe "Test Door"
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180

# In the yard the door is the goal itself.
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
expect [Lockpicking
click action 0
choose 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect Door unlocked
expect-verb unlock_door
quit
